#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059508 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a10cafc6-9da7-5ffc-a0c7-686a7638fbd9" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 2x2 Augmented Matrix to REF Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/id #uuid "0a9e6824-677a-5fae-9867-1701e7d8378f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4697" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2y=0 \\\\ y=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=1$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+2(1)=0 \n\t\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad\n\tx=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=1.$ Or, in vector form, $\\left<  -2,1 \\right>.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059509 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07abc1cc-5794-51a6-bad4-40565eae52be" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/id #uuid "1eea81be-26d7-57dd-a622-d66300de7f4f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4698" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x+5y=5 \\\\ x-6y=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-5y=-5 \\\\ y=-10,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-10$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-5(-10)=-5 \n\t\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad\n\tx=-55.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-55$ and $y=-10.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -55,-10 \\rangle.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306369 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a10cafc6-9da7-5ffc-a0c7-686a7638fbd9" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 2x2 Augmented Matrix to REF Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d0c7ac1-6ca9-598f-b680-73f9d6ab6ac6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -11\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=19$ and $y=-11$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306371} {:answer/id #uuid "e74442d2-c095-5141-b4bc-4f058c3f434a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 14\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=13$ and $y=14$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306372} {:answer/id #uuid "e2efb109-af41-5b60-bfe1-ab972c90eb29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 11\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=10$ and $y=11$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306373} {:answer/id #uuid "4b5ee1b4-fd0c-5324-8b7a-eabfeb4505a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 13\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=11$ and $y=13$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306374} {:answer/id #uuid "0d7dc191-62bd-5a73-9efe-0624f55a97ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -16\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=17$ and $y=-16$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d0c7ac1-6ca9-598f-b680-73f9d6ab6ac6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -11\\end{aligned}],$\n$\\,x=19$ and $y=-11$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306371} :answer-field/id #uuid "fef724db-7e02-5ac7-859f-fd32828736c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306370}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6b8bb874-c303-5f60-b208-8afd16f62899" :question/math-academy-id "q-1059" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system represented by the matrix." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+1\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-1\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -11\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y=8 \\\\  & y=-11,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-11$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(-11)=8\\,⇒\\,x=8+11=19.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=19$ and $y=-11.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306376 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a10cafc6-9da7-5ffc-a0c7-686a7638fbd9" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 2x2 Augmented Matrix to REF Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "807b9363-8553-5f5e-93f3-837ca514ec79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306378} {:answer/id #uuid "db31c201-3ebf-5632-a83f-7785bc6865af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306379} {:answer/id #uuid "a03c748b-522e-5201-9ffb-4302373be61a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 8 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306380} {:answer/id #uuid "b3ea5721-7f8d-5aab-b3e1-04a3f052bbcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306381} {:answer/id #uuid "91dfd4c1-1b7f-54f2-ab9f-2be452da8383" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3ea5721-7f8d-5aab-b3e1-04a3f052bbcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306381} :answer-field/id #uuid "56ffb72d-6588-50f8-8e5c-157ca702bdff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306377}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dc5530a8-d7bb-5ee6-b842-11178cec4e06" :question/math-academy-id "q-130909" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 3 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form using the standard algorithm for Gaussian elimination, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 3 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060126 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07abc1cc-5794-51a6-bad4-40565eae52be" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd273c5e-2100-516a-b1ef-2768979e5d61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306398} {:answer/id #uuid "a541204d-7ddb-5553-a580-d02c2fb7b13c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306399} {:answer/id #uuid "abb243af-5edd-5945-b0a7-d75535ece67b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306400} {:answer/id #uuid "158cd92e-2094-50c1-a678-7f06cd107c5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306401} {:answer/id #uuid "da59ba7a-cac4-51b9-95f0-8e3a0af7c4b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306402}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abb243af-5edd-5945-b0a7-d75535ece67b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306400} :answer-field/id #uuid "853d1717-7599-56c0-8795-a2bd5f10af9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306397}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a63289e5-22c0-55e8-8542-9af2656af30b" :question/math-academy-id "q-20496" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x+7y=-5 \\\\  & 7x+11y=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 7 & 11 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 7 & 11 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 7 & 11 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{27}{2} & \\frac{27}{2}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{2}{27}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{7}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186306403 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07abc1cc-5794-51a6-bad4-40565eae52be" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "140d9992-5054-56b7-a950-081ea449f8c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306405} {:answer/id #uuid "7f53a4ca-9a3e-53f7-8760-a5ed2fe41d61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306406} {:answer/id #uuid "40b38b43-671f-57d0-82b2-57e7cb1c052b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306407} {:answer/id #uuid "c6f0ee00-58fd-5e72-b7b7-3d98b5938b6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306408} {:answer/id #uuid "f82967e3-bea4-5147-8380-6a1895e8304d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306409}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "140d9992-5054-56b7-a950-081ea449f8c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306405} :answer-field/id #uuid "85300939-19fc-5c5a-9662-e314a8e5b7f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306404}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "26bbee69-6c8f-5073-bf18-e5b7229f3605" :question/math-academy-id "q-73538" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 3x-2y=4 \\\\  & 2x-y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 2 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
